diff --git a/website/docs/user-guide/configuration.md b/website/docs/user-guide/configuration.md
index 5f2062ae5e..56f5884c6c 100644
--- a/website/docs/user-guide/configuration.md
+++ b/website/docs/user-guide/configuration.md
@@ -3760,7 +3760,7 @@ kanban:
 
 Kanban requirements select a class/tier or capability, never an exclusive concrete model or provider. `kanban_create(model="class:deep", provider="auto")` and `hermes kanban create --model class:deep --provider auto` request a class; leaving the selector unset uses dynamic default routing. Concrete IDs, concrete providers, mandatory flags, positive `require_model` directives and named-model mandates are rejected at mutation boundaries, including review handoffs. Interactive chat model selection is unchanged.
 
-Legacy and synced concrete restrictions are ignored for future admission, without changing a running agent's client or rewriting its concrete execution receipts. Clear stored restrictions with `hermes kanban set-model <id> none --no-mandatory`; this affects future dispatch only. The dispatcher dynamically chooses a qualified reviewer in a genuinely separate execution/session with authenticated exact-head approval custody. Model attribution is audit history, not an exclusion: the same model may perform an independent review in a separate execution. No eligible route or missing execution/approval custody must fail closed, not be worked around by pinning a reviewer. Subscription reserve, quota, billing, capability and safety gates remain in force. A concrete chosen route in a current-run receipt is execution evidence, not a persistent card restriction.
+Legacy and synced concrete restrictions are ignored for future admission, without changing a running agent's client or rewriting its concrete execution receipts. Each non-dry dispatcher tick also retires stored restrictions on up to 64 open cards belonging to that gateway (including running and review cards), rotating through the board. Class selectors and `auto` providers remain; concrete selectors/providers and mandatory-pin flags are cleared with an audit event and dispatcher comment. Done/archived cards and foreign executor copies are not edited. Refused body lines alone become `Historical run instruction (superseded and not active): <JSON string>` evidence, preserving every other byte and the original line endings. The ordinary field-level sync path propagates these edits to replicas. Concurrent supported edits win the retirement compare-and-swap. Operators can also clear stored restrictions with `hermes kanban set-model <id> none --no-mandatory`; worker shells remain write-fenced. These edits affect future dispatch only. The dispatcher dynamically chooses a qualified reviewer in a genuinely separate execution/session with authenticated exact-head approval custody. Model attribution is audit history, not an exclusion: the same model may perform an independent review in a separate execution. No eligible route or missing execution/approval custody must fail closed, not be worked around by pinning a reviewer. Subscription reserve, quota, billing, capability and safety gates remain in force. A concrete chosen route in a current-run receipt is execution evidence, not a persistent card restriction.
 
 `kanban.pin_quota_reroute_min_hours` (default `6`) remains a legacy compatibility setting for the old concrete-pin reroute helper's wall threshold. Model-neutral admission ignores legacy concrete pins before route selection, so this threshold does not delay or restrict dynamic class selection and cannot restore mandatory model routing. Do not set a concrete task selector to use this compatibility helper.
 
